#: {{syn|en|dependability}}
#: {{ant|en|unreliability}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 April 5|author=Philip Haigh|title=Comment: Pay deal a positive result|journal=RAIL|issue=980|page=3|text=Above all, rail needs to be boring. By that, I mean that it must run its timetable reliably, day-in and day-out. Punctuality and '''reliability''' remain the bedrock of a successful railway.}}
# {{lb|en|education}} the ability to measure the same thing consistently (of a [[measurement]] indicating the degree to which the [[measure]] is consistent); that is, repeated measurements would give the same result (See also [[validity]]).
# {{lb|en|engineering}} measurable time of work before failure

